.TH tapectl-key-escrow-kit 1  "tapectl-key-escrow-kit " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-key\-escrow\-kit \- Generate the printed Heir Kit and the encrypted catalog bundle (ADR\-0005 / ADR\-0009, issue #69)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl key escrow\-kit\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] <\fB\-\-out\fR> [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate the printed Heir Kit and the encrypted catalog bundle (ADR\-0005 / ADR\-0009, issue #69).
.PP
Writes three files: COVER.txt (the plain\-text cover sheet — the artifact with the decades\-scale claim), escrow\-kit.html (the same content with an inline QR, for printing), and catalog.db.age (the whole catalog encrypted to the escrow recipient).
.PP
This command stops at the files. Printing them, sealing them into tamper\-evident envelopes and distributing them across at least two independent failure domains is the operator\*(Aqs part, and the cover sheet states those requirements. Re\-run after each production write session; `audit` warns when the kit has fallen behind the tapes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Directory to write the kit into (created if absent, mode 0700)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
